    "## 4. PyTorch Tensor Basics (Lesson 2.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "Tensors are the fundamental data structure of deep learning. Every weight, every activation, and every gradient inside Qwen3 is a tensor. Let's verify that we can create tensors and move them between CPU and GPU."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a tensor on CPU\n",
    "cpu_tensor = torch.randn(3, 4)  # 3 rows, 4 columns of random floats\n",
    "print(f\"CPU Tensor Shape: {cpu_tensor.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"CPU Tensor Device: {cpu_tensor.device}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Move it to GPU\n",
    "gpu_tensor = cpu_tensor.to(\"cuda\")\n",
    "print(f\"GPU Tensor Device: {gpu_tensor.device}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Matrix multiplication on GPU (this is what every Transformer layer does)\n",
    "weight_matrix = torch.randn(4, 2).to(\"cuda\")\n",
    "result = gpu_tensor @ weight_matrix  # Y = X · W\n",
    "print(f\"Result Shape: {result.shape} (3 tokens × 2 dimensions)\")\n",
    "print(\"\\n✅ GPU tensor math working perfectly!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
