    "---\n",
    "# Module 6 — Supervised Fine-Tuning\n",
    "\n",
    "We have reached the capstone. We have our dataset loaded into Hugging Face `datasets` from Module 5. Now we will load Qwen3-0.6B with 4-bit quantization, inject LoRA adapters, format the dataset using ChatML, train the model, validate its personality, and push it to the Hugging Face Hub."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 20. Model Loading & LoRA Injection (Lesson 6.1)\n",
    "\n",
    "We load the model using Unsloth's optimized `FastLanguageModel`. We use 4-bit NF4 quantization to compress the 600M parameters from 2.4GB down to ~400MB. Then we inject LoRA adapters into the attention projections (`q_proj`, `k_proj`, etc.). We will only train these tiny adapters, leaving the base model weights completely frozen."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"🔄 Loading model with 4-bit quantization...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4-bit NF4 quantization: 600M params compressed from 2.4 GB → ~0.4 GB\n",
    "model, tokenizer = FastLanguageModel.from_pretrained(\n",
    "    model_name     = MODEL_ID,\n",
    "    max_seq_length = MAX_SEQ_LEN,\n",
    "    load_in_4bit   = True,\n",
    "    dtype          = None,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Inject LoRA adapters (ΔW = B × A)\n",
    "model = FastLanguageModel.get_peft_model(\n",
    "    model,\n",
    "    r               = 16,\n",
    "    target_modules  = [\"q_proj\", \"k_proj\", \"v_proj\", \"o_proj\", \"gate_proj\", \"up_proj\", \"down_proj\"],\n",
    "    lora_alpha      = 16,\n",
    "    lora_dropout    = 0.0,\n",
    "    bias            = \"none\",\n",
    "    use_gradient_checkpointing = \"unsloth\",\n",
    "    random_state    = 42,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "trainable = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters() if p.requires_grad)\n",
    "total     = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())\n",
    "vram      = torch.cuda.memory_allocated() / (1024**3)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Model loaded. Trainable: {trainable:,} / {total:,} params ({trainable/total*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"   VRAM used: {vram:.2f} GB\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 21. ChatML Dataset Mapping (Lesson 6.2)\n",
    "\n",
    "The SFTTrainer needs the dataset formatted as raw text tokens, not JSON objects. We inject the ChatML template into our tokenizer and map it across the entire dataset. This flattens our `messages` list into a single string formatted with `<|im_start|>` and `<|im_end|>` tokens."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from unsloth.chat_templates import get_chat_template\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply ChatML template to the tokenizer\n",
    "tokenizer = get_chat_template(\n",
    "    tokenizer,\n",
    "    chat_template = \"chatml\",\n",
    "    mapping = {\"role\": \"role\", \"content\": \"content\", \"user\": \"user\", \"assistant\": \"assistant\"},\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "def formatting_prompts_func(batch):\n",
    "    return {\"text\": [\n",
    "        tokenizer.apply_chat_template(convo, tokenize=False, add_generation_prompt=False)\n",
    "        for convo in batch[\"messages\"]\n",
    "    ]}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Format the dataset using Apache Arrow multiprocessing\n",
    "formatted_dataset = hf_dataset.map(formatting_prompts_func, batched=True, remove_columns=hf_dataset.column_names)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Dataset formatted. {len(formatted_dataset)} training rows ready.\")\n",
    "print(\"--- Row 0 Preview ---\")\n",
    "print(formatted_dataset[0][\"text\"][:300] + \"...\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 22. The Training Loop (Lessons 6.3 - 6.4)\n",
    "\n",
    "We configure the `SFTTrainer`. Crucially, we use `train_on_responses_only()` so the model's loss is calculated ONLY on the assistant's responses, not the user prompts. We set a low learning rate (2e-4) and run the training loop. Watch the loss curve drop!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import time\n",
    "from transformers import TrainingArguments\n",
    "from trl import SFTTrainer\n",
    "from unsloth.chat_templates import train_on_responses_only\n",
    "\n",
    "training_args = TrainingArguments(\n",
    "    output_dir                  = \"./sahur-checkpoints\",\n",
    "    per_device_train_batch_size = 2,\n",
    "    gradient_accumulation_steps = 4,          # Effective batch size = 8\n",
    "    warmup_steps                = 5,\n",
    "    max_steps                   = 60,         # Set to 300-500 for a real run\n",
    "    learning_rate               = 2e-4,\n",
    "    fp16                        = not torch.cuda.is_bf16_supported(),\n",
    "    bf16                        = torch.cuda.is_bf16_supported(),\n",
    "    logging_steps               = 1,\n",
    "    optim                       = \"adamw_8bit\",\n",
    "    weight_decay                = 0.01,\n",
    "    lr_scheduler_type           = \"linear\",\n",
    "    seed                        = 42,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "trainer = SFTTrainer(\n",
    "    model              = model,\n",
    "    tokenizer          = tokenizer,\n",
    "    train_dataset      = formatted_dataset,\n",
    "    dataset_text_field = \"text\",\n",
    "    max_seq_length     = MAX_SEQ_LEN,\n",
    "    dataset_num_proc   = 2,\n",
    "    packing            = False,\n",
    "    args               = training_args,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply response-only masking\n",
    "trainer = train_on_responses_only(\n",
    "    trainer,\n",
    "    instruction_part = \"<|im_start|>user\\n\",\n",
    "    response_part    = \"<|im_start|>assistant\\n\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🚀 Starting training...\")\n",
    "t0 = time.time()\n",
    "stats = trainer.train()\n",
    "elapsed = time.time() - t0\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Training complete in {elapsed/60:.1f} min.\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Final loss: {stats.training_loss:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 23. Inference & Behavioral Validation (Lessons 6.5 - 6.6)\n",
    "\n",
    "The model is trained. Now we switch it to inference mode (which fuses the LoRA adapters in memory for speed) and run a personality regression test to ensure Sahur's tone, slang, and emoji policies were successfully learned."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Switch to inference mode\n",
    "FastLanguageModel.for_inference(model)\n",
    "\n",
    "def sahur_respond(user_message, max_tokens=200):\n",
    "    msgs = [\n",
    "        {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SAHUR_SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n",
    "        {\"role\": \"user\",   \"content\": user_message}\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    prompt = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(msgs, tokenize=False, add_generation_prompt=True)\n",
    "    inputs = tokenizer(prompt, return_tensors=\"pt\").to(model.device)\n",
    "    plen   = inputs[\"input_ids\"].shape[1]\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        out = model.generate(**inputs, max_new_tokens=max_tokens, do_sample=True,\n",
    "                             temperature=0.8, top_k=50, top_p=0.9, use_cache=True)\n",
    "    return tokenizer.decode(out[0][plen:], skip_special_tokens=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Personality regression test suite\n",
    "PROBES = [\n",
    "    (\"Tone\",              \"my python script isn't working\"),\n",
    "    (\"Humor\",             \"why does git push keep rejecting my commits\"),\n",
    "    (\"Friendliness\",      \"this is too hard, i give up\"),\n",
    "    (\"Slang Calibration\", \"what is a python list comprehension\"),\n",
    "    (\"Emoji Policy\",      \"explain async await in python\"),\n",
    "    (\"Verbosity\",         \"what does len() do\"),\n",
    "    (\"Explanation Style\", \"explain recursion to me\"),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(\"🔬 PERSONALITY REGRESSION TEST\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "for dimension, prompt in PROBES:\n",
    "    response = sahur_respond(prompt)\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n[{dimension}]\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Prompt:   {prompt}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  Response: {response[:160]}...\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)"
   ]
  },
